# nrf52840_boot.resc — Renode non-radio boot smoke test
#
# Attempts to load the nRF52840 platform + the firmware ELF and start the CPU.
#
# CRITICAL LIMITATION: The S340 SoftDevice binary is NOT loaded, and the S340
# radio subsystem is NOT emulated by Renode (see README.md for details).
#
# What this script does: loads the ELF into flash, starts the CPU, and lets it
# run long enough to observe the early boot path (clock init, timer init) before
# the first nrf_sdh_enable_request() call blocks on the missing SoftDevice.
#
# For this to reach the USB-CDC heartbeat, the SoftDevice entry points must be
# stubbed behind a HAL: intercept SVC calls that dispatch to the S340 and return
# NRF_SUCCESS / NRF_ERROR_SOFTDEVICE_NOT_ENABLED as appropriate.

$name?="nrf52840-smoke"
using sysbus
mach create $name
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl

# Load the application ELF.
# NOTE: the S340 SoftDevice .hex is NOT loaded — Renode cannot run it.
sysbus LoadELF @../../firmware/_build/nrf52840_xxaa.out

# Hook the RTT peripheral so NRF_LOG output (SEGGER RTT channel) is captured.
# USB-CDC via app_usbd is not modelled, but RTT is the default NRF_LOG backend.
showAnalyzer sysbus.rtt

# Set up a Python hook to intercept SVC calls at the S340 entry point.
# The firmware calls nrf_sdh_enable_request() which issues SVC with the
# SoftDevice enable request. Without the S340 binary loaded, this SVC handler
# is not present and the CPU will HardFault.
#
# Renode's nRF52840 model does not include a pre-loaded SoftDevice, so every
# SoftDevice API call must be intercepted. The Python hook below catches the
# SVC exception and returns NRF_SUCCESS to unblock the boot path.
#
# In practice, a full HAL is needed to stub:
#   nrf_sdh_enable_request, nrf_sdh_disable_request, nrf_sdh_is_enabled,
#   nrf_sdh_ble_enable, nrf_sdh_ble_*_cfg_set, nrf_sdh_ant_enable,
#   sd_ble_gap_*, sd_ble_gattc_*, sd_ble_gatts_*, sd_ant_*, sd_softdevice_*,
#   sd_ecb_block_encrypt, sd_app_evt_wait, sd_clock_hfclk_request, etc.
#
# For this smoke test, we trap the first HardFault and report what happened.

# Start the simulation
start

# Let the CPU run for a few seconds — the ELF will boot through log_init()
# and timers_init() before stalling on softdevice_init().
sleep 5

# Stop and report
echo "=== Boot smoke complete ==="
echo "The firmware loaded successfully. If it reached softdevice_init() and"
echo "hard-faulted on the S340 SVC, that is EXPECTED — see README.md."
echo "CPU registers at stop:"
sysbus.cpu GetArchitectureString
sysbus.cpu PC
